  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Integration: displacement and distance travelled</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 4.2: Find when a body is at rest, its displacement by integration, and the distance travelled by splitting at the time of rest.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Section C, Question C2 in Chapter 1 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Mechanics 1 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: a calculus version with a velocity formula, a new Kenyan context and new numbers.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
